---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const page = {
  title: "How to verify a bootable USB drive — Bootable",
  description: "Understand publisher checksum verification, raw byte read-back, Windows boot-tree audits, and the limits of bootable USB verification.",
  ogTitle: "How Bootable verifies USB media",
  ogDescription: "Checksums before writing, target read-back after writing, and honest verification limits.",
  ogType: "article",
  current: "guide",
  doc: { label: "Validation", href: "https://github.com/debpalash/bootable/blob/main/docs/validation.md" },
  crumbs: [{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Guides", href: "/guides.html" }, { label: "Verify USB media" }],
};
---
<Layout {...page}>
<main class="guide-main">
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={page.crumbs} />
      <article>
        <header class="guide-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Checksums · read-back · boot tree</p><h1>Know what “verified” means.</h1><p class="lede">Bootable checks the download and the written media separately. The result names what was tested and what was not.</p></header>
        <div class="guide-body">
          <div class="guide-content">
            <h2 id="download">1. Download verification</h2>
            <p>When a catalog publisher provides a checksum sidecar or manifest, Bootable associates it with the image and selects the strongest supported digest: SHA-512, SHA-256, SHA-1, or MD5. A mismatch blocks the image from being written.</p>
            <p>If no publisher checksum is available, Bootable records the download as HTTPS-only instead of presenting it as publisher-verified.</p>

            <h2 id="raw">2. Raw write verification</h2>
            <p>During a raw ISO, IMG, or RAW write, Bootable hashes the exact byte stream sent to the device. It flushes the target, reads the same byte range back, and compares SHA-256.</p>
            <p>Compressed sources are compared after expansion. The target must match the decompressed image bytes, not the smaller archive.</p>

            <h2 id="windows">3. Windows media verification</h2>
            <p>Windows installer media is a constructed filesystem rather than a raw copy. Bootable validates the source tree before erasure, then checks the finished UEFI boot files, Windows payload, split WIM sequence, and FAT32 file-size rules.</p>

            <h2 id="limits">What these checks do not prove</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>They do not prove that an operating-system installation will complete.</li>
              <li>They do not guarantee compatibility with every firmware or board revision.</li>
              <li>A checksum proves agreement with the published digest; it is only as trustworthy as the source of that digest.</li>
              <li>Read-back covers the written range. It does not certify unused capacity on a larger drive.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="guide-callout"><p><strong>A failed or cancelled verification is not a warning to ignore.</strong> Treat the media as incomplete and perform a full rewrite.</p></div>

            <h2 id="boot-test">Boot validation</h2>
            <p>The repository includes a separate read-only QEMU/OVMF smoke-test harness for developers. It can confirm that firmware reached a loader frame. It remains separate from physical-media verification and does not claim that setup finished.</p>

            <section class="related-guides"><h2>Related guides</h2><ul><li><a href="/write-iso-to-usb">Write and read back an ISO</a></li><li><a href="/compressed-image-writer">Verify expanded compressed images</a></li><li><a href="/safe-usb-writer">Review the destructive-write safety gates</a></li></ul></section>
            <div class="guide-cta"><h2>Make verification part of the write</h2><p>Bootable reports verification in the same workflow as writing.</p><a class="button primary" href="/download">Download Bootable</a></div>
          </div>
          <aside class="guide-aside"><strong>On this page</strong><ul><li><a href="#download">Download checksum</a></li><li><a href="#raw">Raw read-back</a></li><li><a href="#windows">Windows boot tree</a></li><li><a href="#limits">Limits</a></li><li><a href="#boot-test">Boot validation</a></li></ul></aside>
        </div>
      </article>
</main>
</Layout>
